scenario.en:
process.on('SIGTERM', () => {
  server.close(() => process.exit(0));
});

The pod has a livenessProbe on GET /healthz and a readinessProbe on GET /ready. Neither endpoint changes its response on SIGTERM — /ready always returns 200. There is no preStop hook. During a rolling deploy this pod receives SIGTERM.

Which probe, if it failed, would KILL this pod vs DE-ROUTE it? And without a readiness flip, what do clients see for the few seconds right after SIGTERM?

